Subject: [PATCH 20/20] Android: leave window moves to the desktop caption

Patchy's menu bar doubles as a title bar on frameless desktop windows:
pressing on its empty space restores a maximized window under the
pointer and starts a move, and a double-click toggles maximize. On
Android the menu bar sits under the system caption, which moves and
maximizes the window itself, so each press there shrank the main window
to its normal size inside the app window until it was put back (a
visible flash). Treat no part of the menu bar as a drag area there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/ui/main_window.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ui/main_window.cpp b/src/ui/main_window.cpp
index 150ba10..887c0eb 100644
--- a/src/ui/main_window.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/main_window.cpp
@@ -7816,6 +7816,15 @@ bool MainWindow::eventFilter(QObject* watched, QEvent* event) {
     }
 
     const auto is_chrome_drag_area = [this, bar](const QPoint& position) {
+#ifdef Q_OS_ANDROID
+      // The desktop caption over the menu bar moves and maximizes the window
+      // itself; restoring the main window here would shrink it inside the app
+      // window.
+      Q_UNUSED(this);
+      Q_UNUSED(bar);
+      Q_UNUSED(position);
+      return false;
+#endif
       if (bar->actionAt(position) != nullptr) {
         return false;
       }
